  "source_relationship": "Original Claude generic effect intent adapted to current original Frame and Armor pass2; no reference-decompiled source or artwork.",
  "features": [
    "Claude-authored face-shaded Minecraft voxel sphere/line/ribbon/billboard, adapted to current nested GL Frame instead of a global toggle.",
    "Each effect frame owns 256/1024/2048 cubes by detail; each primitive at most384. Finite input/point/size/step bounds and whole-shape sampling.",
    "Native admitted own WeaponPulse CAST emits original role-specific chips/shards/embers/frost/sparks once per actual entity identity. Native admitted own FIRE shots emit at most once every two observed native ticks. No input-intent or server gameplay changes.",
    "One shared client particle engine for armor and weapons: max600 live; armor lane128 with16new/native tick; weapon lane472 with64new/native tick; fire watchers128, pending and receipts512 each.",
    "World/body/connection identity or native tick rewind clears all caches. Catchup capped4ticks. Pending admission requires exact current world entity-map identity and nondead entity; loaded-block-only bounce checks.",
    "Armor pass2 remains opt-in FALSE; charge, overload, hit spray, heartbeat, steam and night support remain. Shared engine preserves signed gravity/integration order, fixed armor size/fade and additive blend; weapons retain normal blend/shrink. At most2bounded particle batches.",
    "Jutsu detail0, HUD reduced motion or Quiet suppress extra particles and animated armor embellishments through optional reflection; no hard HUD dependency.",
    "Only project-owned carriers/renderers are modified. Original installed providers, NPC assets/icons/armor layers, native chakra, damage, attributes and moves remain authoritative.",
    "Additional raw authored renderer families adapted with a global 1200/3000/9000 generic cube ceiling shared across nested effects and particles, strict native world LOD, native-tick bounded scroll trails and observed-only combat camera feedback. See RUNTIME-RENDERER-016-INTEGRATION.json."
  ],
